article en "Reusable validation of local source declarations"
body
  cons paragraph
    cons sentence
      cons code "SourceAdmission::checked_source_set"
      cons text " returns an immutable borrow of an owned "
      cons code "SourceStore"
      cons text " containing exactly the supplied local declarations, never the admission ledger's union."
      nil
    cons " The returned lifetime belongs to the admission ledger."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Admission and duplicate rejection remain mandatory."
    cons sentence
      cons text " "
      cons code "SourceSetError::Duplicate"
      cons text " denotes a repeated local SourceId/revision; "
      cons code "SourceSetError::Source"
      cons text " retains source conflict and budget stop errors."
      nil
    cons " Admission precedes duplicate detection on a miss."
    cons " A cache hit requires budgeted exact equality of every declaration in the same sequence."
    cons " Independently decoded snapshots are not trusted by digest alone."
    cons " Empty, reordered or changed local sets remain distinct inputs."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "This is a declaration check, not a portable validation receipt or proof of graph, registry, view, mapping, symbol or rendering correctness."
    cons " Callers preserve their operation's cumulative Budget and SourceAdmission."
    cons " Cache replacement completes only after source-set construction succeeds."
    cons " A later consumer failure may leave this valid local set cached, but all consumer-specific checks still run on retry."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Math structural validation uses this exact local store after finalized-registry and shape checks."
    cons " Origins, maps, node locations, views and embedded syntax retain their independent checks."
    cons " The store borrow ends before embedded guests require mutable admission."
    cons sentence
      cons text " Duplicate errors remain "
      cons code "StructureError::DuplicateSource"
      cons text "; source errors and sticky stop reasons retain their existing typed conversion."
      nil
    nil
  nil
